  "name": "Document Q&A API with Citations, Cache and Confidence Gate",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f295a433-e9ce-43c4-8c64-0e689a1f615b",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -672,
        688
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1149,
        "content": "## Document Q&A API with Citations, Cache and Confidence Gate\n\nA POST endpoint that answers questions about your own PDF library and returns\nthe answer, the exact passage it came from, the page number, and clickable\nGoogle Drive links to every source file. Built to be called by a website chat\nwidget, a Slack bot, or any front end that can send JSON.\n\n### How it works\n\nThe webhook validates the request first and returns a 400 when the question is\nmissing, so bad calls never reach a paid model. A repeated question is served\nfrom an answer cache held in an n8n data table, which keeps a busy endpoint\nfast and cheap for seven days. New questions go to a retrieval agent that\nsearches a Pinecone index through OpenAI embeddings, reranks the matches with\nCohere, and returns structured JSON: the answer, a confidence number, and one\ncitation per supporting passage. A confidence gate sits after the agent, so a\nweak or unsupported answer comes back as an honest not-found response rather\nthan a guess. Good answers have their source file names deduplicated, looked\nup once each in Google Drive, and turned into view and download links, with\nany file missing from Drive named in the reply. Every answer is then cached,\nwritten to an audit log with its confidence and response time, and returned.\nConversation memory keyed on the caller's session id makes follow-up questions\nwork.\n\n### Setup\n\nAdd your OpenAI, Gemini, Pinecone, Cohere, Drive and Sheets credentials. Point\nthe Knowledge Base node at your Pinecone index, create a data table with the\ncolumns named on the cache node, and set the sheet ID and QA Log tab.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the cache window, the confidence threshold, or the reranker topN to\ntrade accuracy against cost."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
